FEATURE: changelog-requirement
DATE: 2026-08-26
SCOPE: require ChangeLog.md to be updated for every change, and backfill what was missed
FOLLOWS: changelog/example-design-standard

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AFFECTED PROJECTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

vUX library (this repository) — conventions and release notes only.

  - CLAUDE.md      change-logging section now names four places, not three
  - ChangeLog.md   thirteen entries backfilled across Added, Fixed and Changed

No source, documentation or example file changed.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The user observed that ChangeLog.md was not being updated. It was not: the three features
completed before this one wrote their per-feature logs under changelog/<feature>/ and left
the root file untouched.

The instruction allowed it. The change-logging section scoped the whole obligation to
"./changelog/<feature-Name>/", and ChangeLog.md was named only under "## Reference", as a
file to consult before assuming an old API name — never as one to write. Following the
section literally produced exactly the omission that was reported.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT CHANGED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

CLAUDE.md's change-logging section now counts four places instead of three and names
ChangeLog.md as the fourth, distinguishing the two records by audience: ChangeLog.md is
release-facing and read by consumers, the per-feature logs are the internal working
record, and neither substitutes for the other. It carries the style rules the file's
existing entries follow — consumer's point of view, present tense, no dates or file paths
except where a file is the deliverable, new bullets rather than edits to old ones — and
ends with the completion criterion stated outright, since the heading's "required for
every change" had not been sufficient on its own.

ChangeLog.md gains three Added bullets, eight Fixed bullets covering the fifteen AutoWriter
defects, and two Changed bullets, all under the existing v4.0.0-beta headings.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VERIFICATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ChangeLog.md's structure is unchanged — the same version heading and the same four
category headings, with bullets appended to three of them and no existing line rewritten.
